{
  "background_and_question": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Rivers",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "2b97ff6b76054c9ac57e987676a8ec6a7d32c1bbfa6ffc51042e7a2b4555a8b5",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-2b97ff6b7605-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 12,
              "start": 12
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Rivers argues that his filing does not trigger the requirements of \u00a72244(b) because it was submitted while his first habeas petition was still on appeal."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Rivers",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "2b97ff6b76054c9ac57e987676a8ec6a7d32c1bbfa6ffc51042e7a2b4555a8b5",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-2b97ff6b7605-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 12,
              "start": 12
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Rivers, the legal question is whether Rivers's filing constitutes a second or successive habeas petition under \u00a72244(b) of the AEDPA."
      }
    ],
    "heading": "Background & Question",
    "status": "complete",
    "summary": null,
    "summary_citations": []
  },
  "case_id": "scotus-23-1345",
  "decision": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "2b97ff6b76054c9ac57e987676a8ec6a7d32c1bbfa6ffc51042e7a2b4555a8b5",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-2b97ff6b7605-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 12,
              "start": 12
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Court does not agree with Rivers's proposition that his filing is not a second or successive application."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "2b97ff6b76054c9ac57e987676a8ec6a7d32c1bbfa6ffc51042e7a2b4555a8b5",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-2b97ff6b7605-0001-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 12,
              "start": 12
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Whether a filing qualifies as a second or successive application generally turns on the existence of a final judgment on the first petition, not the status of an appeal."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "2b97ff6b76054c9ac57e987676a8ec6a7d32c1bbfa6ffc51042e7a2b4555a8b5",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-2b97ff6b7605-0001-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 13,
              "start": 13
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Such filings are not themselves properly considered to be second or successive applications under AEDPA."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "2b97ff6b76054c9ac57e987676a8ec6a7d32c1bbfa6ffc51042e7a2b4555a8b5",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-2b97ff6b7605-0001-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 18,
              "start": 18
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "A second\u2011in\u2011time \u00a72254 petition generally qualifies as a second or successive application, triggering the requirements of \u00a72244(b), when an earlier filed petition has been decided on the merits and a judgment exists."
      }
    ],
    "heading": "Decision",
    "status": "complete",
    "summary": null,
    "summary_citations": []
  },
